  "notes": "{配線|はいせん} refers to electrical wiring or the act of wiring.\n\nCOMPOSITION:\n- {配|はい}: To distribute, arrange\n- {線|せん}: Wire, line\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {配線|はいせん}する (to wire, to install wiring)\n- {配線|はいせん}{工事|こうじ} (wiring work)\n- {配線|はいせん}{図|ず} (wiring diagram)\n- {電気|でんき}{配線|はいせん} (electrical wiring)\n- {屋内|おくない}{配線|はいせん} (indoor wiring)\n- {配線|はいせん}を{引|ひ}く (to run wiring)\n\nRELATED TERMS:\n- ケーブル (cable)\n- コード (cord)\n- {電線|でんせん} (electric wire)\n- {回路|かいろ} (circuit)\n\nREGISTER: Neutral. Technical vocabulary commonly used in construction, IT, and everyday contexts.",
